Alembic migrations for My Life.

The database URL and target metadata are provided by migrations/env.py from the
application settings (MYLIFE_DATABASE_URL; local default = SQLite). Domain models
register on mylife.db.base.Base and must be importable from env.py so autogenerate
and `alembic check` see them.

Common commands (run from the repository root):

  alembic upgrade head                    # apply all migrations
  alembic revision -m "add X" --autogenerate
  alembic downgrade -1                     # roll back one revision
  alembic check                           # fail if models drift from migrations

CI runs `alembic upgrade head` followed by `alembic check` to guarantee the
migrations stay in sync with the models.
